<title>JAPAN: Japan May platinum imports down 21.2 pct yr/yr-MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan May platinum imports down 21.2 pct yr/yr-MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's platinum imports in May were down 21.2 percent from a year earlier at 4.96 tonnes, Finance Ministry data released on Friday showed.  </p>
<p>		The figures were as follows (in kg):</p>
<p>		    May 97	Apr 97	 May 96</p>
<p> Total	    4,960	 6,078	   6,290</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Russia	     804	 2,834	   2,390</p>
<p> South Africa   3,284	   954	   3,140</p>
<p>Cumulative imports in the first five months of 1997 amounted to 27.24 tonnes, down from 30.10 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7431</p>
</text>
